If you feel that casting negates polymorphism, then fair enough. I can 
see what you mean; but I feel that polymorphism is a concept rather than 
a syntactical structure. It means that more than one object type can be 
used in the same place, without need for knowledge of the actual type of 
object. This concept is not negated by requiring a cast to a base type. 
(But it sure is a hell of a lot uglier.)

